From 14163d7b5ae62b357545fb63e1617b44213c6caf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunrisepeak <speakshen@163.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 04:02:31 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tidy): const range fixes use semantic constraint checks

The mutation analyzer examines the instantiated non-const program. Const iterator declarations and forwarding adaptor templates can therefore appear read-only even when their const constraints are unavailable. The previous operator-pipe heuristic also hid valid ordinary user-pipe suggestions.

Provide the current Sema to tidy AST checks in both clang-tidy and clangd. Probe concrete member range iteration and free pipe consumption with an isolated const lvalue, in the original declaration context and an unevaluated scope. Preserve lookup qualifiers and explicit template arguments, and restore provisional diagnostic suppression with RAII. Detect errors from deduced-return body instantiation without leaking them into the original program. Regression cases cover unavailable and available dependent constraints, mutable references, ordinary pipes, private iteration and a failing provisional static assertion followed by a real warning.
